  "_comment": "Maps territory names in the border snapshots to data entities. 'aliases' maps a border NAME to an ISO3 code or to a key in 'historical' (a value can also be a list of {until, code} rules for names that mean different places in different years, or {partOf: ISO3} for a territory that is only part of a modern state: it gets no data of its own and links to that state). Names not listed are matched to modern countries automatically by scripts/build-borders.mjs. A historical entity's data comes from its own code first (e.g. SUN for the USSR in Maddison and Polity); 'proxy' names a successor whose data is shown instead, with 'note' explaining the approximation. Without a proxy the panel says no data exists for that entity and lists its successors.",
